# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Open Harness Hub .gitignore
#
# Goal: never accidentally stage generated factory output, local reference
# clones, or OS/tooling cruft. Curated, published outputs are negated back in.
#
# Note: already-tracked files stay tracked regardless of these rules. To add a
# new file under an ignored path on purpose, use `git add -f <path>`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- MkDocs build output ---
/site/

# --- Local reference repos ---
# Cloned for offline study only; NEVER republished (AGENTS.md hard rule).
# Tracked gitlink pointers remain; their working-tree contents stay out.
/_reference/

# --- Generated factory output (dist/) ---
# Ignored by default so daily run scratch (which can reach gigabytes) is never
# staged by accident. Curated, published emitter products are negated back in
# below. Keep this negation list as the single source of truth for "which dist
# outputs are products, not scratch" (see docs/codex/no-magic-values.md).
/dist/*
!/dist/agent-skills/
!/dist/aibom/
!/dist/c2pa/
!/dist/croissant/
!/dist/hf/
!/dist/lm-eval-harness/
!/dist/mcp/
!/dist/openlineage/
!/dist/promptfoo/
!/dist/spdx/
!/dist/catalog.sqlite

# Private/internal docs (acquihire material, internal strategy) — NOT part of the open-core publication
docs/internal/
